   "page": 1,
   "source": "tesseract-psm3",
   "text": "Origin\nThe breeder is F Hannemann of Box Hill North, Victoria.\nThis variety arose from a controlled pollination in 1986 of\nthe miniature rose \u2018Oz Gold\u2019 by the shrub rose \u2018Eyepaint\u2019.",
   "text_format": "plain",
   "type": "text"
  },
  {
   "bbox": [
    305.28,
    114.48,
    540.0,
    231.48
   ],
   "id": "e7",
   "lines": [
    {
     "bbox": [
      306.72,
      114.48,
      463.32,
      123.48
     ],
     "text": "Morphology \u2014 see comparison tables."
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      306.36,
      124.56,
      527.4,
      132.48
     ],
     "text": "\u2018Cecilia\u2019 is a low bi-coloured cluster-flowered rose with"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      306.0,
      134.28,
      527.76,
      142.56
     ],
     "text": "flowers larger than those of \u2018Cream Puff\u2019 and similar in"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      306.0,
      143.64,
      536.76,
      153.36
     ],
     "text": "size to \u2018Summer Breeze\u2019. The undulating thick petals give"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      306.0,
      154.08,
      515.16,
      162.72
     ],
     "text": "the ftower a cupped appearance similar to \u2018Summer"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      306.0,
      163.8,
      518.76,
      172.44
     ],
     "text": "Breeze\u2019 but unlike the flat shape of \u2018Cream Puff\u2019. The"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      306.0,
      173.88,
      540.0,
      183.24
     ],
     "text": "appearance of the flower can be compared with the larger"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      306.0,
      184.32,
      527.76,
      192.96
     ],
     "text": "shrub roses \u2018Fruhlingsmorgen\u2019 and \u2018Sparrieshoop\u2019. The"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      305.64,
      194.04,
      516.6,
      203.4
     ],
     "text": "foliage is matt and of a lighter green than that of the"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      305.28,
      204.48,
      505.08,
      213.12
     ],
     "text": "comparative varieties. The stipules of \u2018Cecilia\u2019 are"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      305.64,
      214.56,
      508.32,
      223.56
     ],
     "text": "significantly shorter than those of the comparative"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      305.28,
      225.0,
      340.56,
      231.48
     ],
     "text": "varieties."
    }
   ],
   "page": 1,
   "source": "tesseract-psm3",
   "text": "Morphology \u2014 see comparison tables.\n\u2018Cecilia\u2019 is a low bi-coloured cluster-flowered rose with\nflowers larger than those of \u2018Cream Puff\u2019 and similar in\nsize to \u2018Summer Breeze\u2019. The undulating thick petals give\nthe ftower a cupped appearance similar to \u2018Summer\nBreeze\u2019 but unlike the flat shape of \u2018Cream Puff\u2019. The\nappearance of the flower can be compared with the larger\nshrub roses \u2018Fruhlingsmorgen\u2019 and \u2018Sparrieshoop\u2019. The\nfoliage is matt and of a lighter green than that of the\ncomparative varieties. The stipules of \u2018Cecilia\u2019 are\nsignificantly shorter than those of the comparative\nvarieties.",
   "text_format": "plain",
   "type": "text"
  },
